                         USER EXPERIENCE
The five things I would protect most carefully
If we're optimizing for a cheap but technically strong Mobbin alternative, these are the architectural assets I would consider most important:
1. Immutable raw evidence — lets us reprocess everything as our models improve.
2. Unified design graph — prevents web/iOS/Android from becoming separate systems.
3. Automated exploration + state deduplication — determines how much useful data we can collect without human labor.
4. Multimodal indexing — text + metadata + visual + component + flow search.
5. Incremental crawling/change detection — determines whether the economics work at scale.
The actual screenshot crawler is comparatively straightforward. The difficult and valuable part is turning millions of heterogeneous captures into a clean, deduplicated, versioned, searchable design dataset.
That is the architecture I would build around.
